  "description": "Our lightest mountain bike is our engineering heavyweight. The PSYCHO PATH 1 makes that perfectly clear. The racing-oriented carbon frame with a starting weight of 1,100g provides top performance in every situation. A competitive seating position sets the bar high, while the 29” wheel set ensures speed and control (27,5” in size S). With the SRAM SX Eagle we’ve assembled a group that can play with the big boys (in terms of technology) while also being cost-effective. The Shimano MT4100 is destined for competitions and the trail. Its strength lies in the precise brake modulation which provides awesome stopping power and high reliability. The Rock Shox Judy Silver TK suspension fork in the Boost Solo Air variety with a Maxle Stealth axis offers you terrific feedback and gives you full control even on challenging terrains. * approx. 12,1 kg, may vary by up to +/- 5% due to manufacturing tolerances, weight for splash blue frame, size M, without pedals",
